    text: "---"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 015.4 — the discovery"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Tidecaller Sanctuary & Regional Giant Territories"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 10,550, month 2, day 14"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Torhh, Pazuzu, Saresh, Giant tribal leaders"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: Torhh and Pazuzu discover the Ash Giants' collaboration via unencrypted Anunnaki Needle broadcasts; the revelation drives the remaining tribes into permanent isolation, fulfilling Queen Eduhauana's multi-millennial strategy to shatter indigenous trust."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: 34 days after the Ash Giant vote in scene 015.3"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: Transmission of the Ash Giant betrayal across the Needle network and the total collapse of inter-tribal trust."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "The other tribes learned of the betrayal through Needle surveillance that the Anunnaki ensured wasn't encrypted."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "The message was blunt: \"Ash Giant territories secured through cooperative arrangement."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Intelligence sharing commencing."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "Recommended application: additional pressure on remaining resistant factions.\""
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "Torhh received the notification through consciousness-channels that centuries of Needle maintenance had made familiar, and felt something ancient break in its awareness."
  - line: 36
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They chose them,\""
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "the Tidecaller rumbled to Pazuzu, who stood beside the ancient Giant as they had for three thousand years. \"After everything. After the Garden. After the First Coming's resistance. After we suffered together in the convergence. They looked at their pain and decided cooperation with the golden ones was preferable to alliance with us.\""
  - line: 39
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Pazuzu
    text: "\"We blamed them,\""
  - line: 41
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"So this is our fault?\""
  - line: 43
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"This is the Queen's design, executed perfectly across three thousand years of patient manipulation. She planted lies that isolated them. She deployed Gruulith specifically to break them. She knew the ritual would fracture alliances along existing suspicions. And she calculated that when we blamed them for requiring rescue, they would hear confirmation that they had always been separate, always been judged, always been alone.\""
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Torhh's ocean-deep eyes carried grief that geological patience couldn't absorb."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "\"The other tribes are already fragmenting further."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "The Forest Giants withdraw to their territories, certain that any cooperation makes them vulnerable to similar betrayal."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "The Mountain clans hoard their knowledge more tightly, trusting no one."
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "The Subterranean populations—already isolated—see confirmation that surface alliances are impossible.\""
  - line: 51
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Pazuzu
    text: "\"And the Sundering is complete,\""
  - line: 53
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Can it be healed? In time, can we—\""
  - line: 55
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Pazuzu
    text: "\"No,\""
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "In the northern mountains, Ash Giants were accepting Anunnaki healing treatments, providing intelligence on other tribal movements, allowing Needle infrastructure to be maintained through their territories without resistance."
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "In the southern deserts, Saresh and the survivors were retreating into the deepest chambers, certain that surface cooperation led only to betrayal."
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "In the forests and highlands and subterranean depths, tribes were calculating isolation as the only viable strategy, each convinced that the Ash Giants' choice proved what three thousand years of subtle programming had suggested: other factions could not be trusted when pressure became sufficient."
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "The Nephilim had completed their purpose—eliminated Anunnaki creatures, fulfilled cosmic law's requirements for balance."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "They departed as efficiently as they'd manifested, their consciousness returning to quantum foam, their forms dissolving back into the vrill-energy from which they'd been constructed."
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "They left behind Giants who had summoned defenders through unified suffering, and emerged too fractured to defend each other."
  - line: 68
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "Year 10,550, Month 6, Day 21"

